# Architecture

Clean Architecture with rigid layer boundaries.

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend | `apps/web` | RSC by default; `'use client'` only for interactive UI |
| Presentation | `apps/api/app/api/` | Routers `/api/v1/`, Pydantic validation, JWT, CORS |
| Domain/Service | `apps/api/app/services/` | Credits, scoring, RAG, ingestion — no FastAPI imports |
| Repository | `apps/api/app/repositories/` | Async SQLAlchemy persistence only |
| Tasks | `apps/api/app/tasks/` | Celery: PDF parse, embeddings, batch AI generation |

## Tenancy

- Every request that reads/writes tenant data must resolve `organization_id` (header `X-Organization-Id` or personal org).
- Never leak rows across organizations. Filter in the repository, not only in the router.
- RBAC roles: `owner`, `admin`, `member`, `auditor`.

## API conventions

- Versioned routes only: `/api/v1/...`
- JWT access tokens; payload includes `sub` (user id) and optional `org_id`.
- Long work (PDF, AI) is always Celery; API returns `202` + job status, never blocks on LLM calls.
